Servlet = Servlet is a client side java technology used to provide dynamic responses to the Clients.
To use Servlet first you need to download "Apache Tomcat" from https://tomcat.apache.org/. 
after downloading you have to configure Apache Tomcat server on your respective browser.
You can provide static response to user just simply using index.html 
but if you want to provide dynamic resonses (which changes according to user) you have to use servlet 

Servlet Lifecycle =
1. The servlet container loads the servlet class into memory.
2. After loading the class, the container creates an instance, which will be reused for all upcoming requests.

3. init() method used only one time for the entire servlet life used for tasks like to open the database connections.
ex public void init(ServletConfig config) throws ServletException

4. service() method called for every client request which creates request and response object for each request.
ex public void service(ServletRequest req, ServletResponse res)
    throws ServletException, IOException

5. destroy() method called once when the servlet is being removed from service 
ex public void destroy()
